docs {
  The exception/processing center. Every request here requires an admin
  token: system_admin holds both incident:read and incident:manage.

  There are no happy-path requests here for acknowledge, resolve, add-note,
  set-severity, assign-owner or request-replay — the same limitation
  admin/folder.bru documents for DLQ replay, one level further down: an
  incident only exists after internal/incident.Watcher merges a real dead
  letter into one, and a dead letter only exists after a consumer exhausts
  its retries. Neither is a thing an HTTP client can trigger on demand, so
  this collection cannot produce a real incident to act on. Those six
  operations are each still exercised once, honestly, as a 404 against a
  well-formed but non-existent id — see errors/incident-*-not-found.bru —
  which is what TestEveryDocumentedOperationHasARequest requires and all
  this collection can truthfully offer. The happy path for all six, plus
  the merge/dedup rule and the real (not assumed) replay-result resolution,
  is covered by internal/incident's unit and real-Postgres integration
  tests instead.

  list-incidents and get-incidents-summary answer meaningfully on a fresh
  database: an empty exception center is items: [] and counts: {}, not an
  error.
}
